<aside><h1>Web Based Parking</h1><p>Folio3 Parking is one responsive web app. Employees sign in with Google, register vehicles, manage dedicated-space releases and claim temporary availability. Parking Administrators manage employee parking records, settings, access/report recipients, and utilization. Keep employee and administrator navigation separate and consistent within each role. Use compact, orderly SaaS/workforce patterns: plain navigation, small readable type, hairline dividers, restrained surfaces, status lozenges, tight tables, and no oversized hero areas. Let the product design system determine all colours and fonts. Every page must work at phone, tablet, and desktop widths; use touch-sized controls on narrow screens.</p><h3>Screens</h3><ul><li><a href="#S-1">S-1 <code>/sign-in</code></a></li><li><a href="#S-2">S-2 <code>/parking</code></a></li><li><a href="#S-3">S-3 <code>/parking/available</code></a></li><li><a href="#S-4">S-4 <code>/parking/releases</code></a></li><li><a href="#S-5">S-5 <code>/parking/vehicles</code></a></li><li><a href="#S-6">S-6 <code>/admin</code></a></li><li><a href="#S-7">S-7 <code>/admin/employees</code></a></li><li><a href="#S-8">S-8 <code>/admin/parking-settings</code></a></li><li><a href="#S-9">S-9 <code>/admin/access-reports</code></a></li><li><a href="#S-10">S-10 <code>/admin/utilization</code></a></li></ul><h3>No screen</h3><ul><li><b>REQ-1</b> When a person submits a Google OAuth callback, the Folio3 Parking web app shall create an authenticated session only after validating the Google-issued ID token signature, issuer, and audience, verifying OAuth state, and confirming that the account belongs to an active Folio3 employee. <i>(no screen: The sign-in page starts Google OAuth and shows failure states, but validating the Google ID-token signature, issuer and audience, verifying OAuth state, and creating a session only after active-employee checks are server-side callback/security operations; the callback itself is not a separate user-facing page.)</i></li><li><b>REQ-5</b> Where deployment bootstrap configuration is used, the Folio3 Parking web app shall keep initial administrator setup incomplete until configuration supplies a designated active Folio3 account, then grant that account the initial Parking Administrator role, and allow Parking Administrators to configure the daily release time, per-floor space counts, work calendar, named report recipients, and administrator and Security Guard role assignments. <i>(no screen: The initial administrator grant is deployment bootstrap behavior: setup stays incomplete until configuration identifies a designated active Folio3 account, then grants that account the first Parking Administrator role. The administrator pages cover settings and subsequent role configuration; no separate page is needed for the deployment-time grant.)</i></li><li><b>REQ-14</b> When a released parking allocation becomes claimable, the Folio3 Parking web app shall send an email notification using a fixed template to eligible employees without dedicated parking who have a registered vehicle. <i>(no screen: The fixed-template email is an automated notification sent when a released allocation becomes claimable; email delivery is not a page in the web app.)</i></li><li><b>REQ-15</b> If a permanently stickered vehicle arrives, then the Folio3 Parking web app shall leave its existing sticker process unaffected and preserve any temporary claim already made for that date, including when configured capacity is exceeded. <i>(no screen: Preserving the existing permanent-sticker process and any temporary claim when a stickered vehicle arrives is an integration/allocation rule, not a user-facing page.)</i></li><li><b>REQ-16</b> When the Folio3 LPR integration submits an entrance-verification request, the Folio3 Parking web app shall authenticate the request as originating from trusted Folio3 LPR equipment, require a unique authenticated request ID or nonce and reject any previously accepted ID or nonce, then verify a detected car&#39;s readable plate against that date&#39;s temporary parking authorizations and activate the green indicator only for a valid authorization. <i>(no screen: Authenticating trusted LPR equipment, requiring a unique authenticated request ID or nonce, rejecting replayed IDs/nonces, checking the detected readable plate against that date’s temporary authorizations, and activating the indicator only for valid authorization are equipment-integration operations with no human page.)</i></li><li><b>REQ-17</b> If any entrance verification fails, then the Folio3 Parking web app shall issue an explicit command to set the green indicator inactive and deny entry through the temporary-parking process. <i>(no screen: On every failed entrance verification, explicitly deactivating the green indicator and denying temporary-parking entry is a fail-safe integration command, not a user-facing page.)</i></li><li><b>REQ-18</b> The Folio3 Parking web app shall record every successful and unsuccessful entrance verification attempt with its timestamp, plate when readable, result, and entry status. <i>(no screen: Entrance verification attempts must be persisted with timestamp, readable plate when available, result, and entry status. This is automatic audit recording; the requirement does not ask for a separate entrance-attempt page.)</i></li><li><b>REQ-19</b> The Folio3 Parking web app shall record daily utilization events using registered-vehicle entry records, counting an allocation as used when any vehicle registered to its employee is detected that day. <i>(no screen: The background use-counting rule—count an allocation as used when any vehicle registered to its employee is detected that day—is automatic event processing. Its statistics and records are shown in the Utilization page.)</i></li><li><b>REQ-20</b> When the weekly reporting job runs on Monday morning in the Folio3 office time zone, the Folio3 Parking web app shall generate a report containing unused dedicated and temporary parking, daily and weekly utilization statistics, released-space and claim totals, and an overall utilization percentage calculated for the reporting week as 100 times used allocations divided by eligible allocations, or 0 percent when there are no eligible allocations. <i>(no screen: The Monday-morning office-time-zone job that compiles weekly statistics and unused dedicated/temporary parking is scheduled report generation. The resulting report is shown in the Utilization page; the scheduler has no page of its own.)</i></li><li><b>REQ-21</b> Where a Parking Administrator has configured a named report-recipient list, the Folio3 Parking web app shall send weekly employee-identifying report emails only to configured recipients who have the Parking Administrator role, omitting all other listed addresses from delivery. <i>(no screen: Filtering the named report-recipient list at delivery time so that employee-identifying report emails go only to configured recipients with the Parking Administrator role is backend mail-delivery enforcement. The configured list and eligibility are shown in Access &amp; Reports.)</i></li><li><b>REQ-22</b> The Folio3 Parking web app shall provide filterable on-screen lists and CSV export of utilization records only to Parking Administrators, and deny both operations to callers in every other role. <i>(no screen: The Utilization page serves authorized administrators. Enforcing denial of both utilization-list and CSV operations for every other role is an access-control rule, not a separate page.)</i></li><li><b>REQ-23</b> The Folio3 Parking web app shall retain parking-release audit history, LPR verification attempts, and utilization events according to Folio3&#39;s existing records-retention policy. <i>(no screen: Applying Folio3’s existing records-retention policy to parking-release audit history, LPR attempts, and utilization events is an automatic retention operation and has no page of its own.)</i></li></ul></aside>
